how-to/How-to-generate-R-plots-for-Bench.content:
R is a framework to generate graphics and computations.
To use it to generate graphics for BenchmarkDotNet you have to follow these steps:

download R from the official website (yes, I know, the website does not look fancy…);
install it, and store somewhere the installation path (for me, C:\Users\d.bellone\AppData\Local\Programs\R\R-4.3.2 );
set the enviroment variable on Windows. For some reasons, I couldn’t edit the values, so I came up with the next steps;
run the benchmarks
open the BenchmarkDotNet.Artifact folder under the bin of your project. For me it’s under \bin\Release\net8.0\BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts. You should see some .log files;
ensure that in the result subfolder you have some CSV files and, more important, a file named BuildPlots.R;
open a terminal in the results folder, and run this command: C:\Users\d.bellone\AppData\Local\Programs\R\R-4.3.2\bin\RScript.exe ./BuildPlots.R;

Now you should see lots of PNG files with the rendering of the results.
Who generates those CSV? If you remember from before, we customized every benchmark with the [Config(typeof(CsvConfig))] attribute. This attribute generates both the CSV and the R files, and is defined like this:
 public class CsvConfig : ManualConfig
 {
     public CsvConfig()
     {
         Add(CsvMeasurementsExporter.Default);
         Add(RPlotExporter.Default);
     }
 }
